  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved the best performance so far (acc=0.591, F1=0.573), a ~10.6% gain over the singleprofile baseline (config_001, acc=0.485). Image-only models are weak (0.21-0.23), confirming RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We have only tested avgpool as the multiprofile aggregation method; it is unknown whether a transformer-based aggregation would better capture inter-profile interactions and further improve performance. This experiment (config_003) isolates the aggregation variable by changing only avgpool→transformer while keeping rna_only, multiprofile, and pca_n2000 fixed, making it a clean A/B comparison against config_002. It is the best next step because it directly exploits the current best direction with a minimal, interpretable change; the result will inform whether more complex aggregation is warranted before investing compute in multimodal fusion experiments, and it reduces uncertainty about a core architectural choice that would propagate into all future multimodal configurations."
}

